---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import registry from '../../generated/registry.json';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const generated = new Date(registry.generated as string).toISOString().slice(0, 10);
---

<Base title="What changed — Vermont School Budgets">
  <h1>What changed</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Every change to this site's data, formulas, and sources is saved as a commit. This page shows
    them, so the history of what changed and when is out in the open — not something you have to
    take on trust.
  </p>

  <div class="notice">
    <strong>Nothing here yet</strong>
    <p>
      This page is built from the project's save history — nightly list updates, new number files,
      and data fixes. It fills in as those happen. The site was built on
      {generated}, so there is no history to show yet beyond that.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>What will appear here</h2>

  <h3>Master-list updates</h3>
  <p>
    Each night, a job compares the Agency of Education's directory against our master list and
    opens a request whenever they differ — never merging on its own, so every change in Vermont's
    school setup gets read by a person and a note explaining it. As a bonus, that record becomes a
    public history of district reorganization, which nobody else is publishing right now.
  </p>

  <h3>New number files</h3>
  <p>
    Each time a legal number is checked against the current law, or the Legislature changes one,
    a new number file is released and shows up here with its sources. The consultant advice on
    special education, sparsity, high-school, and career-tech weights will come as a new file
    rather than an edit to an old one, so you can still see both the before and the after.
  </p>

  <h3>Corrections</h3>
  <p>
    When a number here turns out to be wrong, the fix is a saved change like any other and it
    shows up on this page. That is on purpose. A site that quietly edits its mistakes is asking
    for more trust than one that leaves the record visible — and it deserves less.
  </p>

  <p>
    See also <a href={`${base}/methodology/`}>how it works</a>, which shows whether each number
    has been checked yet.
  </p>
</Base>
